The upstream has no NOTICE file; this attribution notice was added by API-MRI (formerly relay-audit).
Vendored Python changes: attribution header and package-relative imports only.
API-MRI (formerly relay-audit) reuses the upstream probes, prompts, parser, consensus labels, domain
tolerances, validation and statistical scoring. Its own HTTP transport uses
timeouts, cancellation, credential redaction, truncation checks and replay validation.
Thinking discovery questions are reproduced with attribution in fingerprint.py.
Each of six discovery strategies is tried at most once; each batch has at most
three format attempts, no automatic network retries, and no 50x token fallback.
